      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the adult man from <Picture 1>, wearing a navy overshirt over a white T-shirt and charcoal trousers. The four views show one person's identity, not multiple people. He has a warm, natural Mandarin-speaking voice (S1).\n<Subject 2> is the adult woman from <Picture 2>, with shoulder-length wavy dark hair, a cream cardigan and small gold earrings. The four views show one person's identity. She has a clear, gentle Mandarin-speaking voice (S2).\n<Subject 3> is the restaurant interior from <Picture 3>, retaining the wooden table, green upholstered seating, warm brass lamps and soft window light.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] A 14-second live-action restaurant scene in one continuous shot. A man and a woman greet each other, share a quiet dining moment, then raise their water glasses and toast. All dialogue is in Mandarin Chinese.\n\nretention_analysis:\nPreserve both characters' facial identities, hairstyles and clothing throughout. Keep the man on screen left and the woman on screen right. Retain the restaurant's lighting, furniture and table arrangement. Begin with the composition of the supplied first frame. Only these two people are visible. Maintain the same camera axis throughout the shot.\n\ndetailed_description:\n[Shot 1] A cinematic medium two-shot frames both seated characters, their faces, hands, plates and separate water glasses. The man sits on screen left, facing the woman on screen right. The camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed throughout the scene, keeping both characters and their glasses visible. Warm window light softly illuminates their faces. The entire scene unfolds continuously without cuts.\n\nFrom 0.00 to 3.00 seconds, the man raises his gaze toward the woman, smiles and gives a small nod. The man (S1) says warmly: <d>[Chinese] 你好！</d> The woman looks at him and listens, with natural blinking and her lips closed.\n\nFrom 3.00 to 5.00 seconds, the woman's smile becomes brighter. She gently nods toward him. The woman (S2) replies: <d>[Chinese] 见到你真高兴。</d> The man listens quietly, maintaining eye contact without speaking.\n\nFrom 5.00 to 8.00 seconds, the man looks down at his plate, lifts one small bite of food with his fork and brings it to his mouth. He chews with his mouth closed, lowers the fork and looks back toward the woman. She watches him with a relaxed smile. Neither person speaks during this interval.\n\nFrom 8.00 to 11.00 seconds, the woman reaches for her own water glass and lifts it to chest height. Looking at the man, the woman (S2) says invitingly: <d>[Chinese] 我们干一杯吧。</d> The man looks toward her raised glass. Their glasses remain apart during this interval.\n\nFrom 11.00 to 14.00 seconds, the man picks up his own water glass. The man (S1) answers cheerfully: <d>[Chinese] 干杯！</d> Both extend their glasses toward the center of the table. At approximately 12.50 seconds, the glass rims touch once, producing one clear, delicate clink. They then draw their glasses slightly back and keep holding them while smiling at each other through the final frame.\n\nEach quoted line is spoken exactly once by its assigned speaker. Mouth movements follow the spoken words naturally. The listener remains silent. Breathing, blinking and small facial reactions continue between actions. No subtitles or other on-screen text appear.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nQuiet, continuous restaurant ambience with faint off-screen dining sounds. Clear foreground Mandarin dialogue, one speaker at a time. Soft fork-and-plate contact during 5.00–8.00 seconds, followed by one distinct glass clink at approximately 12.50 seconds. No narration.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A",
